---
id: migrate-from-v1
title: Migrating from v1
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Form v2 keeps the same core idea as v1: create a form with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useForm"},{"type":"text","value":", render fields from the returned form API, and submit with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.handleSubmit()"},{"type":"text","value":". Most migrations are not a full rewrite, but v2 does\nchange several React-facing APIs that show up in examples and integration\ntests."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This page is a starting checklist for migrating React apps from v1 to v2."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"quick-checklist","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quick checklist"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useForm"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.Field"},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":", but update render props from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.state.value"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.state.meta"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.value"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.meta"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Always provide "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useForm"},{"type":"text","value":". v2 does not support omitting\nthem."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Move field-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValue"},{"type":"text","value":" props into form-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Remove field-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" props. Model initial validation and error\nvisibility through validators, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runOnMount"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errorVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Change validation from keyed event objects like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ onChange, onBlur }"},{"type":"text","value":" to\narrays of validator objects with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"run"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggers"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Change async validator debounce options such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChangeAsyncDebounceMs"},{"type":"text","value":" to\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggerDebounceMs"},{"type":"text","value":" on the validator object."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Change field cross-validation from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChangeListenTo"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onBlurListenTo"},{"type":"text","value":" to\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"watchFields"},{"type":"text","value":" on validators or listeners."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mode=\"array\""},{"type":"text","value":" fields with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.ArrayField"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep array mutations on the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ArrayField"},{"type":"text","value":" render prop, such as\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"array.pushValue(...)"},{"type":"text","value":", or use path-based form methods such as\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.pushFieldValue(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" when the control lives outside the render prop."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rename "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.moveFieldValues"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.moveFieldValue"},{"type":"text","value":", and replace removed\nform methods such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setFieldMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validateField"},{"type":"text","value":" as described in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"#removed-and-renamed-form-methods","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Removed and renamed form methods"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read errors from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.errors"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group.state.errors"},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.state.errors"},{"type":"text","value":" as validation issue objects. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error.message"},{"type":"text","value":" when\nrendering text."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In form- and group-level validators, build routed errors with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createErrorMap(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" and return the map directly."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createValidationError(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":" when a submit handler\nneeds to route server errors back to form or field state."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSelector"},{"type":"text","value":", which replaces v1's deprecated "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useStore"},{"type":"text","value":" usage."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Subscribe to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.atom"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.atom"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.store"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.store"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"formOptions(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" for shared base form options."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withForm"},{"type":"text","value":" components with plain components that accept a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form"},{"type":"text","value":" prop\ntyped as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReactFormType<typeof formOpts>"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useFormGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.FormGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" for scoped sections of the same\nform."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withFieldGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineFieldGroup(...).bindComponent(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" for\nreusable field bundles that map virtual field names to different concrete\nform paths."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Upgrade Vue to version 3.6 or newer when using the Vue adapter. Form\nComposition relies on behavior introduced in Vue 3.6."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Update CommonJS integrations to consume ESM. The v2 packages do not publish\na CommonJS build and require Node.js 18 or newer."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Upgrade React to version 18 or newer. The v2 React adapter no longer supports\nReact 17."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Update CommonJS integrations to consume ESM. The v2 packages do not publish\na CommonJS build and require Node.js 18 or newer."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"react-version","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React version"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The v2 React adapter supports React 18 and 19. React 17 is no longer supported,\nso upgrade "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"react"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"react-dom"},{"type":"text","value":", and their corresponding type packages before\nmigrating. If you imported "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CrossVersionReactNode"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-form"},{"type":"text","value":",\nimport "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReactNode"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"react"},{"type":"text","value":" instead."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"vue-version","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue version"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The v2 Vue adapter requires Vue 3.6 or newer. At the time of writing, Vue 3.6\nhas not yet been released as stable and is available as a release candidate.\nWe hope Vue 3.6 will be stable by the time TanStack Form v2 becomes stable."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Form Composition relies on Vue 3.6 behavior to work correctly. Requiring it\nfrom the start lets the Vue adapter support Form Composition without adding a\nbreaking minimum-version change later in the v2 release line."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"package-format","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Package format"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The v2 core, framework, devtools, and server-adapter packages publish ESM\nexports only and declare Node.js 18 as their minimum version. Prefer "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"import"},{"type":"text","value":" /\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"export"},{"type":"text","value":" syntax, use dynamic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"import()"},{"type":"text","value":" when consuming them from CommonJS, and\nmake sure any Node-based test, SSR, or build tooling can load ESM dependencies.\nThere is no separate CommonJS build or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"require"},{"type":"text","value":" export to fall back to."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-fields","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic fields"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The v1 simple example and v2 basic example are intentionally similar. The main\nrender-prop difference is that v2 exposes the subscribed field surface directly."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v1\n<form.Field name=\"firstName\">\n  {(field) => (\n    <input\n      name={field.name}\n      value={field.state.value}\n      onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n      onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n    />\n  )}\n</form.Field>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"// v2\n<form.Field name=\"firstName\">\n  {(field) => (\n    <input\n      name={field.name}\n      value={field.value}\n      onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n      onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n      aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\n    />\n  )}\n</form.Field>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same applies to common meta and error reads:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v1\nfield.state.value\nfield.state.meta.isTouched\nfield.state.meta.isValid\nfield.state.meta.errors.join(',')","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"// v2\nfield.value\nfield.meta.isTouched\nfield.meta.isValid\nfield.errors.map((error) => error.message).join(',')","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v2 also exposes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.meta.isInvalid"},{"type":"text","value":", which is the inverse of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isValid"},{"type":"text","value":" and\nis convenient for attributes such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aria-invalid"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The v2 React integration tests also assert that fields rerender independently\nwhen sibling fields change. Prefer reading only the subscribed field values and\nmeta you need in each render prop."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"defaults-and-initial-meta","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defaults and initial meta"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In v1, a form could rely on field-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValue"},{"type":"text","value":" props:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v1\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {} as Person,\n})\n\n<form.Field name=\"firstName\" defaultValue=\"\">\n  {(field) => <input value={field.state.value} />}\n</form.Field>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In v2, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" are required on the form and are the only place to define\ninitial values:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v2\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    lastName: '',\n  },\n})\n\n<form.Field name=\"firstName\">\n  {(field) => <input value={field.value} />}\n</form.Field>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<form.Field defaultMeta={...}>"},{"type":"text","value":" was also removed. If v1 code used\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultMeta={{ isTouched: true }}"},{"type":"text","value":" to show errors immediately, replace the\nimplicit meta state with mount validation and an explicit visibility policy:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v2\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n  },\n})\n\n<form.Field\n  name=\"firstName\"\n  validators={[\n    {\n      runOnMount: true,\n      triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n      run: ({ value }) => (value ? undefined : 'First name is required'),\n    },\n  ]}\n>\n  {(field) => (\n    <>\n      <input\n        value={field.value}\n        onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n        onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n      />\n      {field.errors.map((error) => (\n        <p key={error.message}>{error.message}</p>\n      ))}\n    </>\n  )}\n</form.Field>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If errors should validate on mount but remain hidden until the user blurs the\nfield or tries to submit, use a form-level policy such as\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errorVisibility: ({ fieldState, state }) => fieldState.meta.isBlurred || state.submissionAttempts > 0"},{"type":"text","value":" instead."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"validators","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validators"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v1 validators are keyed by event names:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v1\n<form.Field\n  name=\"firstName\"\n  validators={{\n    onChange: ({ value }) =>\n      !value\n        ? 'A first name is required'\n        : value.length < 3\n          ? 'First name must be at least 3 characters'\n          : undefined,\n    onChangeAsyncDebounceMs: 500,\n    onChangeAsync: async ({ value }) => {\n      await checkName(value)\n      return value.includes('error')\n        ? 'No \"error\" allowed in first name'\n        : undefined\n    },\n  }}\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v2 validators are ordered arrays. Each validator has a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"run"},{"type":"text","value":" function or\nstandard schema, a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggers"},{"type":"text","value":" list, and optional behavior like debouncing or\nbailing:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v2\n<form.Field\n  name=\"firstName\"\n  validators={[\n    {\n      run: ({ value }) => {\n        if (value.length === 0) return 'A first name is required'\n        if (value.length < 3) return 'First name is too short'\n      },\n      triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n      triggerDebounceMs: 300,\n    },\n    {\n      run: async ({ value }) => {\n        await checkName(value)\n        return value.toLowerCase().includes('error')\n          ? 'No \"error\" allowed in first name'\n          : undefined\n      },\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      bailIfInvalid: true,\n    },\n  ]}\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Useful translations:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v2"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validators.onMount"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"validator with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runOnMount: true"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validators.onChange"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"validator with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggers: ['change']"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validators.onBlur"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"validator with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggers: ['blur']"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validators.onSubmit"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"validator with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggers: []"},{"type":"text","value":", or rely on submit running validators by default"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChangeAsync"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"async "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"run"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggers: ['change']"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChangeAsyncDebounceMs"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggerDebounceMs"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChangeListenTo"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onBlurListenTo"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"watchFields"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validationLogic: revalidateLogic()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"migrate to explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggers"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"when"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runOnSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bailIfInvalid"},{"type":"text","value":" rules"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Submission is separate from the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggers"},{"type":"text","value":" list: every validator runs during\nsubmission by default. An empty "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggers: []"},{"type":"text","value":" therefore means \"no change or\nblur validation, but still validate on submit.\" Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runOnSubmit: false"},{"type":"text","value":" when a\nvalidator must not run during client submission; do not add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'submit'"},{"type":"text","value":" to\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggers"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggers"},{"type":"text","value":" can contain strings or trigger config objects. Use config objects\nwhen a validator should only run for some changes:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"validators={[\n  {\n    triggers: [\n      {\n        trigger: 'change',\n        when: ({ value }) => Boolean(value),\n      },\n    ],\n    watchFields: ['startDate'],\n    run: ({ value, formApi }) => {\n      const startDate = formApi.getFieldValue('startDate')\n      if (value < startDate) return 'End date must be after the start date'\n    },\n  },\n]}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Predicate callbacks are scope-aware. A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"when"},{"type":"text","value":" callback, a function-valued\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runOnSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":", or a function-valued "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggerDebounceMs"},{"type":"text","value":" receives "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scope"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"formApi"},{"type":"text","value":"; field predicates receive the field being validated as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fieldApi"},{"type":"text","value":",\nwhile group predicates also receive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"groupApi"},{"type":"text","value":". For form and group predicates,\nan optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fieldApi"},{"type":"text","value":" is the field that triggered validation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createValidator(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" when the scheduling policy should be reused with\ndifferent validator functions or schemas while preserving their inferred\ntypes:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createValidator } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nconst validateAfterSubmit = createValidator({\n  triggers: [\n    {\n      trigger: 'change',\n      when: ({ groupApi, formApi }) =>\n        (groupApi?.state.submissionAttempts ??\n          formApi.state.submissionAttempts) > 0,\n    },\n  ],\n})\n\nconst validators = [validateAfterSubmit(schema)]","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"standard-schemas","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Standard schemas"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v1 accepted standard schemas in event-keyed validators:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v1\nuseForm({\n  defaultValues,\n  validators: {\n    onChange: schema,\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In v2, pass schemas as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"run"},{"type":"text","value":" values inside the validators array:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v2\nuseForm({\n  defaultValues,\n  validators: [\n    {\n      run: schema,\n      triggers: ['change'],\n    },\n  ],\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The form's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":" remains its editable input state. When a Standard Schema\nvalidator runs successfully during submission, its parsed output is available\nin "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":" at the corresponding "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"schemaOutputs"},{"type":"text","value":" index. Non-schema entries\nare "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":". Validators with literal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runOnSubmit: false"},{"type":"text","value":" are skipped during\nsubmission, and their slots are typed as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":". Use the parsed entry when\nan endpoint expects the schema's output type."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For schema-led option inference, pass the schema first and the options second.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"formOptions.strictSchema(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" uses the schema input as the form shape, while\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"formOptions.looseSchema(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" permits editable nullish defaults and combines\nthem with the schema shape. These option helpers only affect types; the\nvalidators still perform the runtime parsing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When manually calling a schema, return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parseIssues(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" with the failed issue\narray. In a field validator it produces field issues; in a form or group\nvalidator it routes issue paths into a form/field map; and in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":" it\nproduces a branded submit validation result. The v2 field-group example uses\nthis helper after calling "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"schema.safeParse(...)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"errors-and-submit-results","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Errors and submit results"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v1 examples commonly render errors from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.state.meta.errors"},{"type":"text","value":". In v2,\nrender from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.errors"},{"type":"text","value":" for fields, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group.state.errors"},{"type":"text","value":" for form groups, and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.state.errors"},{"type":"text","value":" for the form. Each of the group and form collections is an\narray. The items are validation issue objects, so render "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error.message"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"function FieldError({ field }: { field: AnyFieldApi }) {\n  return (\n    <small role={field.meta.isInvalid ? 'alert' : undefined} aria-live=\"polite\">\n      {field.errors.map((error) => error.message).join('\\n')}\n    </small>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Form- and group-level validators can route errors to the form and individual\nfields. Build a map with the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createErrorMap"},{"type":"text","value":" supplied to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"run"},{"type":"text","value":", then return the\nmap itself:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n  },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: ({ value, createErrorMap }) => {\n        const errors = createErrorMap()\n\n        if (!value.firstName.trim()) {\n          errors.form = 'Please correct the highlighted fields'\n          errors.fields.firstName = 'First name is required'\n        }\n\n        return errors\n      },\n    },\n  ],\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createErrorMap"},{"type":"text","value":" also accepts an initial "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ form, fields }"},{"type":"text","value":" object. An empty\nreturned map is treated as a valid result.\nField-level validators continue to return their own issue, string, issue array,\nor a valid result directly."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Submit handlers can now return a typed validation result. Use\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createValidationError"},{"type":"text","value":" to route endpoint errors back into form state:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    lastName: '',\n  },\n  onSubmit: async ({ value, createValidationError }) => {\n    const result = await saveUser(value)\n\n    if (!result.ok) {\n      return createValidationError({\n        form: 'Could not save user',\n        fields: {\n          firstName: 'Name already exists',\n          lastName: 'Name already exists',\n        },\n      })\n    }\n\n    return null\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.handleSubmit()"},{"type":"text","value":" resolves to the validation-result array for that\nsubmission attempt, so framework examples can await it and continue to native\nor server submission when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errors.length === 0"},{"type":"text","value":". A thrown or rejected\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":" marks submission unsuccessful but is not added to that array. Return\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createValidationError(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parseIssues(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" when a submit failure should\nbecome validation state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"selectors-and-atoms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Selectors and atoms"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v1 re-exported "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useStore"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-store"},{"type":"text","value":", but that usage was\ndeprecated before v2. In v2, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSelector"},{"type":"text","value":" and subscribe to atoms:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v1\nimport { useStore } from '@tanstack/react-store'\n\nconst errors = useStore(form.store, (state) => state.errors)\nconst fieldErrors = useStore(field.store, (state) => state.meta.errors)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"// v2\nimport { useSelector } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nconst errors = useSelector(form.atom, (state) => state.errors)\nconst fieldErrors = useSelector(field.atom, (state) => state.meta.errors)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same rename applies when subscribing to field groups:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const values = useSelector(fields.atom, (values) => values)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reading "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.state"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group.state"},{"type":"text","value":" gives an imperative snapshot; it does not\nsubscribe a React component. Use field render props, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group.Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSelector"},{"type":"text","value":" for reactive reads, and keep selectors\nfocused on the state the component renders."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"arrays","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Arrays"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v1 represented array fields with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mode=\"array\""},{"type":"text","value":" and exposed array helpers from\nthe field render prop:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v1\n<form.Field name=\"people\" mode=\"array\">\n  {(field) => (\n    <>\n      {field.state.value.map((_, index) => (\n        <form.Field key={index} name={`people[${index}].name`}>\n          {(subField) => (\n            <input\n              value={subField.state.value}\n              onChange={(event) => subField.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n            />\n          )}\n        </form.Field>\n      ))}\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        onClick={() => field.pushValue({ name: '', age: 0 })}\n      >\n        Add person\n      </button>\n    </>\n  )}\n</form.Field>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v2 uses a dedicated "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.ArrayField"},{"type":"text","value":" component for array subscriptions. Its\nrender prop still exposes array methods, so the direct migration can keep the\nmutation next to the rendered array:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v2\n<form.ArrayField name=\"people\">\n  {(array) => (\n    <>\n      {array.value.map((_, index) => (\n        <form.Field key={index} name={`people[${index}].name`}>\n          {(field) => (\n            <input\n              name={field.name}\n              value={field.value}\n              onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n              onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n            />\n          )}\n        </form.Field>\n      ))}\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        onClick={() => array.pushValue({ name: '', age: 0 })}\n      >\n        Add person\n      </button>\n    </>\n  )}\n</form.ArrayField>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the mutation control is outside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ArrayField"},{"type":"text","value":", use the path-based form API\ninstead:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"form.pushFieldValue('people', { name: '', age: 0 })","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same choice is available for inserting, removing, moving, swapping,\nfiltering, and clearing values: use the relative methods on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"array"},{"type":"text","value":" or the\nfield-path methods on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The v2 array example calls out the performance reason for this change:\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ArrayField"},{"type":"text","value":" lets the array shell rerender when the array structure changes\nwithout forcing the whole list to rerender for every item value change."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For current usage and adapter-specific examples, see "},{"type":"link","href":"./arrays","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Arrays"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"removed-and-renamed-form-methods","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Removed and renamed form methods"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The v2 form API is smaller than v1's. It reads and updates values, mutates\narrays, runs form-level validation, submits, and resets. Field metadata now\nlives on the field API, validators and submit results produce errors instead\nof code writing them directly, and nothing replaces the internal\nfield-registry helpers."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v2"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"moveFieldValues(name, from, to)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"moveFieldValue(name, from, to)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setFieldMeta(name, updater)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setFieldValue"},{"type":"text","value":" update options, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"handleSubmit()"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errorVisibility"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFieldMeta(name)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.meta"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resetFieldMeta(...)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resetField(name)"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.reset()"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reset(form.state.values, { updateDefaultValues: false })"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validateField(name, cause)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"validator "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggers"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"watchFields"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validateAllFields(cause)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"handleSubmit()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validateArrayFieldsStartingFrom(...)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"array methods run change validation unless "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"causeValidation: false"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validate(cause)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validate('change' | 'blur')"},{"type":"text","value":", which runs form-level validators only"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getAllErrors()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.state.errors"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.errors"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.state.isValid"},{"type":"text","value":", or the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"handleSubmit()"},{"type":"text","value":" result"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setErrorMap(errorMap)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"errors returned from validators, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createValidationError(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"serverState"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"deleteField(name)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"removeFieldValue"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterFieldValues"},{"type":"text","value":" for array items, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setFieldValue"},{"type":"text","value":" on the parent object"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFieldInfo(name)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none; it exposed internal field registration"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parseValuesWithSchema(schema)"},{"type":"text","value":" and its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Async"},{"type":"text","value":" variant"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a schema validator plus "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"schemaOutputs"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":", or call the schema directly"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFormGroupMeta(name)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group.state"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.FormGroup"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"field-metadata","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field metadata"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v1 code often wrote field meta directly, for example to mark a field as touched\nwhen its value was set programmatically. In v2, meta is derived from updates.\nPass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FieldUpdateOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setFieldValue"},{"type":"text","value":", the array methods, or\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.handleChange"},{"type":"text","value":" to control what an update marks:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v1\nform.setFieldValue('firstName', 'Ada', {\n  dontUpdateMeta: true,\n  dontValidate: true,\n})\nform.setFieldMeta('firstName', (prev) => ({ ...prev, isTouched: true }))","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"// v2\nform.setFieldValue('firstName', 'Ada', {\n  markAsTouched: true,\n  markAsDirty: false,\n  causeValidation: false,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v1 update option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v2 update option"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dontUpdateMeta"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"markAsTouched: false"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"markAsDirty: false"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dontValidate"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"causeValidation: false"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dontRunListeners"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To touch every field before showing errors, call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.handleSubmit()"},{"type":"text","value":", which\nmarks all registered fields as touched. To show errors without touching fields,\nconfigure "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errorVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" instead."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read meta from the field API, as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.meta"},{"type":"text","value":" in a render prop or with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSelector(field.atom, (state) => state.meta)"},{"type":"text","value":". The form API does not look up\nmeta by path."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To clear meta, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.resetField(name)"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.reset()"},{"type":"text","value":" reset one field's\nvalue and meta. To clear every field's meta but keep the values the user\nentered, reset the form to its current values without moving the default\nbaseline:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"form.reset(form.state.values, { updateDefaultValues: false })","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This also clears form-level errors, submission state, and dirty history."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"on-demand-validation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On-demand validation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v2 has no public method that validates a single field or every field outside\nsubmission. Express when a field validates through its validators instead:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggers"},{"type":"text","value":" to choose the events that run a validator."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"watchFields"},{"type":"text","value":" to rerun a validator when another field changes, which\ncovers most v1 "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validateField"},{"type":"text","value":" calls made from another field's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChange"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.handleSubmit()"},{"type":"text","value":" to validate every field and the form together.\nUnlike "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validateAllFields"},{"type":"text","value":", it also calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":" when validation passes.\nIt resolves to the error results, so an empty array means everything is\nvalid."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.validate('change')"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.validate('blur')"},{"type":"text","value":" still exist, but they run\nform-level validators only. Field validators do not run."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"errors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Errors"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v2 does not write error maps directly. Return errors from a validator, or from\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createValidationError(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" as shown in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"#errors-and-submit-results","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Errors and submit results"}]},{"type":"text","value":". For server-rendered\nerrors, pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"serverState"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useForm"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To read errors, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.state.errors"},{"type":"text","value":" holds form-level errors only. Errors routed\nto fields stay on the fields, available as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.errors"},{"type":"text","value":". Use\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.state.isValid"},{"type":"text","value":" to check both levels at once."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"schemas","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Schemas"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parseValuesWithSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" checked the current values against a schema without\nstoring errors. To keep that behavior, call the schema yourself:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const result = await schema['~standard'].validate(form.state.values)\n\nif (result.issues) {\n  // handle issues\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To validate with the schema and use its parsed output, add it to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validators"},{"type":"text","value":"\nand read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"schemaOutputs"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":", as described in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"#standard-schemas","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Standard schemas"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"shared-form-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shared form options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For extracted components, v1 composition examples often use a custom\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAppForm"},{"type":"text","value":" hook plus "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withForm"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createFormHook"},{"type":"text","value":". v2 still supports app\nform hooks, but "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withForm"},{"type":"text","value":" was removed. The smaller building block for shared\ndefaults is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"formOptions(...)"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { formOptions } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nexport const sharedFormOptions = formOptions({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    lastName: '',\n    address: {\n      street: '',\n      country: '',\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nconst form = useForm({\n  ...sharedFormOptions,\n  onSubmit: ({ value }) => {\n    console.log(value)\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When typing extracted components, prefer the v2 public types covered in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./splitting-forms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Splitting forms"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { AnyReactFormApi, FieldWithValue } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nfunction StringField({ field }: { field: FieldWithValue<string> }) {\n  return (\n    <input\n      value={field.value}\n      onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n    />\n  )\n}\n\nfunction SubmitButton({ form }: { form: AnyReactFormApi }) {\n  return (\n    <form.Subscribe selector={(state) => [state.canSubmit, state.isSubmitting]}>\n      {([canSubmit, isSubmitting]) => (\n        <button type=\"submit\" disabled={!canSubmit || isSubmitting}>\n          {isSubmitting ? '...' : 'Submit'}\n        </button>\n      )}\n    </form.Subscribe>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AnyReactFormApi"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FieldWithValue<T>"},{"type":"text","value":" intentionally erase unrelated type\ndetails for generic UI pieces. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReactFormType<typeof formOpts>"},{"type":"text","value":" when a\ncomponent needs the option-derived data and field-path surface. Options created\nwith "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"appFormOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" also retain their app component map. Submit error types\nmay intentionally widen when the shared options omit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":" so it can be\nsupplied later. Prefer these aliases over spelling the full "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FormApi"},{"type":"text","value":" or\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FieldApi"},{"type":"text","value":" generic lists in application components."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For components that previously used "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withForm"},{"type":"text","value":", pass the form API explicitly and\ntype it from the same options object:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v1\nconst AddressFields = withForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    address: {\n      street: '',\n      country: '',\n    },\n  },\n  render: ({ form }) => (\n    <>\n      <form.Field name=\"address.street\">{/* ... */}</form.Field>\n      <form.Field name=\"address.country\">{/* ... */}</form.Field>\n    </>\n  ),\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"// v2\nimport { formOptions } from '@tanstack/react-form'\nimport type { ReactFormType } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nexport const profileFormOptions = formOptions({\n  defaultValues: {\n    address: {\n      street: '',\n      country: '',\n    },\n  },\n})\n\ninterface AddressFieldsProps {\n  form: ReactFormType<typeof profileFormOptions>\n}\n\nfunction AddressFields({ form }: AddressFieldsProps) {\n  return (\n    <>\n      <form.Field name=\"address.street\">{/* ... */}</form.Field>\n      <form.Field name=\"address.country\">{/* ... */}</form.Field>\n    </>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"form-groups-and-field-groups","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Form groups and field groups"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace v1 form group usage with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.FormGroup"},{"type":"text","value":". It is the v2 tool for\nmulti-step forms and scoped validation when a section is part of one concrete\nform shape:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<form.FormGroup name=\"guestDetails\" onSubmit={() => goToNextStep()}>\n  {(group) => (\n    <>\n      <group.Field name=\"name\">\n        {(field) => (\n          <input\n            value={field.value}\n            onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n          />\n        )}\n      </group.Field>\n      <button type=\"button\" onClick={() => group.handleSubmit()}>\n        Continue\n      </button>\n    </>\n  )}\n</form.FormGroup>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inside the group, field names are scoped. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name=\"name\""},{"type":"text","value":" becomes\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"guestDetails.name"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group.ArrayField name=\"guests\""},{"type":"text","value":" becomes\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"guestDetails.guests"},{"type":"text","value":", and watched fields are scoped the same way."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Group submission is its own validation cycle. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group.handleSubmit()"},{"type":"text","value":" validates\nthe group and its fields and then calls the group's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":" or\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmitInvalid"},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.handleSubmit()"},{"type":"text","value":" does not also run the group's\nvalidators. Keep any rules required for final whole-form submission in the\nform-level validator pipeline as well. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group.handleSubmit()"},{"type":"text","value":" resolves to an\nerror array, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group.state.errors"},{"type":"text","value":" is an array."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a field inside a mounted group, scalar state exposed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errorVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":"\n(such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"submissionAttempts"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isDirty"},{"type":"text","value":") is scoped to the nearest group.\nThe callback's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"values"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errors"},{"type":"text","value":" remain form-wide."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v1's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withFieldGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" HOC was removed. v2 replaces it with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineFieldGroup(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" for reusable field bundles. Use it when a component\nshould not care where its fields live in the parent form:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineFieldGroup } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nconst rangeFieldGroup = defineFieldGroup(({ strict }) => ({\n  lower: strict<string>(),\n  upper: strict<string>(),\n}))\n\nfunction RangeFieldsImpl({\n  fields,\n}: {\n  fields: typeof rangeFieldGroup.fields\n}) {\n  return (\n    <>\n      <fields.Field name=\"lower\">\n        {(field) => (\n          <input\n            value={field.value}\n            onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n          />\n        )}\n      </fields.Field>\n      <fields.Field\n        name=\"upper\"\n        validators={[\n          {\n            triggers: ['change'],\n            watchFields: ['lower'],\n            run: ({ value }) => {\n              const lower = fields.getFieldValue('lower')\n              if (Number(value) < Number(lower)) {\n                return 'Upper bound must be greater than lower bound'\n              }\n            },\n          },\n        ]}\n      >\n        {(field) => (\n          <input\n            value={field.value}\n            onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n          />\n        )}\n      </fields.Field>\n    </>\n  )\n}\n\nexport const RangeFields = rangeFieldGroup.bindComponent(\n  RangeFieldsImpl,\n  'fields',\n)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Then bind virtual names to concrete paths wherever the group is used:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<RangeFields\n  form={form}\n  fields={{\n    lower: 'minPrice',\n    upper: 'maxPrice',\n  }}\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use this v2 pattern to migrate v1 "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withFieldGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" components that were reused\nagainst different field paths. If you are using app form components from\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createFormHook"},{"type":"text","value":", wrap components that expect an injected field API with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFormHookHelpers()"},{"type":"text","value":", then define field groups with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineAppFieldGroup"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createFormHook, getFormHookHelpers } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nconst { fieldComponent } = getFormHookHelpers()\nconst AppTextField = fieldComponent.strict(StringField, 'field')\n\nconst { appFormOptions, useAppForm, defineAppFieldGroup } = createFormHook({\n  fieldComponents: {\n    TextField: AppTextField,\n  },\n  formComponents: {},\n})\n\nconst contactFieldGroup = defineAppFieldGroup(({ strict }) => ({\n  name: strict<string>(),\n}))","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"listeners","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Listeners"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v1 listeners were event-keyed objects. v2 listeners use a validator-like array\nshape with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"run"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggers"},{"type":"text","value":", and optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggerDebounceMs"},{"type":"text","value":". A trigger can be\na string or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ trigger, when }"},{"type":"text","value":", and debounce can be a number or a callback.\nForm listeners support "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"change"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blur"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"submit"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mount"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reset"},{"type":"text","value":"; field\nlisteners additionally support "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unmount"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v2\n<form.Field\n  name=\"amount\"\n  listeners={[\n    {\n      triggers: ['blur'],\n      run: ({ value, fieldApi }) => {\n        fieldApi.handleChange(Number(value).toFixed(2))\n      },\n    },\n  ]}\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For cross-field field listeners, put the source fields in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"watchFields"},{"type":"text","value":". In\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.FormGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" and field-group-bound components, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"watchFields"},{"type":"text","value":" uses the scoped\nor virtual field names and v2 resolves them to the concrete form paths.\nForm-level listeners instead observe propagated events and receive an optional\nsource field as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggerFieldApi"},{"type":"text","value":". It is present for propagated field changes\nand blurs, but absent for form-originated events such as mount, reset, and\nsubmit."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"server-and-framework-integrations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server and framework integrations"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The v1 examples include Next server actions, Remix, and TanStack Start examples\nthat use v1's keyed validators and store-level errors. The v2 examples show a\nnew server-validation model in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-form-start"},{"type":"text","value":" and a Next.js\nexample with shared isomorphic validation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Key changes:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"serverValidateHelper"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-form"},{"type":"text","value":", then import the\nframework adapter from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-form-start"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-form-nextjs"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Share common form configuration with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"formOptions(...)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createErrorMap()"},{"type":"text","value":" map directly from framework/server validators\nwhen routing form and field errors."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Combine "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggers: ['server']"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runOnSubmit: false"},{"type":"text","value":" for a form validator\nthat must run only on the server. Server-triggered validators otherwise still\nrun during client submission because submission is enabled by default."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next.js and Remix adapters, and the Start adapter when no callback override is\nsupplied, resolve to\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ success: true, values, schemaOutputs }"},{"type":"text","value":" or\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ success: false, serverState }"},{"type":"text","value":". Pass the failure's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"serverState"},{"type":"text","value":" back to\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useForm({ ...formOpts, serverState })"},{"type":"text","value":" on the client."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-form-remix"},{"type":"text","value":" was removed."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For example, a Start adapter is configured separately from the shared form\noptions:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { serverValidateHelper } from '@tanstack/react-form'\nimport { start } from '@tanstack/react-form-start'\n\nconst { createServerValidate } = serverValidateHelper({\n  framework: start(),\n})\n\nconst serverValidate = createServerValidate(formOpts)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"formOpts"},{"type":"text","value":", a server-only validator returns its routed error map directly:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{\n  triggers: ['server'],\n  runOnSubmit: false,\n  run: ({ value, createErrorMap }) => {\n    const errors = createErrorMap()\n\n    if (value.age < 13) {\n      errors.fields.age = 'You must be at least 13'\n    }\n\n    return errors\n  },\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client rendering still follows the same v2 field surface:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<form.Field name=\"age\">\n  {(field) => (\n    <>\n      <input\n        name={field.name}\n        value={field.value}\n        onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n        onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(Number(event.target.value))}\n      />\n      {field.errors.map((error) => (\n        <div key={error.message} role=\"alert\">\n          {error.message}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </>\n  )}\n</form.Field>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"migration-order-for-an-app","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migration order for an app"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Upgrade imports and keep the smallest possible form compiling with\nESM "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"import"},{"type":"text","value":" syntax, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useForm"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.Field"},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.handleSubmit()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Move every field-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValue"},{"type":"text","value":" into form-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" and\nremove "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultMeta"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Update field render props from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.state.*"},{"type":"text","value":" to the direct v2 surface."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useStore(...store...)"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSelector(...atom...)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Convert validators and listeners to arrays, paying special attention to the\ndefault submit behavior."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Convert arrays from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mode=\"array\""},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.ArrayField"},{"type":"text","value":"; keep relative\nmutators on its render prop or move them to path-based form methods."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createErrorMap(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" directly from form, group, and server validators,\nand convert submitted endpoint errors to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createValidationError(...)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Revisit composition: use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"formOptions(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" for shared options,\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReactFormType<typeof formOpts>"},{"type":"text","value":" for extracted form props,\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.FormGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" for scoped sections, and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineFieldGroup(...).bindComponent(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" for reusable field bundles."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Re-run React integration tests around validation timing, field rerenders,\ngroups, server error hydration, and array mutations. These are the areas\nwhere v2 intentionally tightened behavior."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"quick-checklist","text":"Quick checklist","level":2},{"id":"react-version","text":"React version","level":2},{"id":"vue-version","text":"Vue version","level":2},{"id":"package-format","text":"Package format","level":2},{"id":"basic-fields","text":"Basic fields","level":2},{"id":"defaults-and-initial-meta","text":"Defaults and initial meta","level":2},{"id":"validators","text":"Validators","level":2},{"id":"standard-schemas","text":"Standard schemas","level":2},{"id":"errors-and-submit-results","text":"Errors and submit results","level":2},{"id":"selectors-and-atoms","text":"Selectors and atoms","level":2},{"id":"arrays","text":"Arrays","level":2},{"id":"removed-and-renamed-form-methods","text":"Removed and renamed form methods","level":2},{"id":"field-metadata","text":"Field metadata","level":3},{"id":"on-demand-validation","text":"On-demand validation","level":3},{"id":"errors","text":"Errors","level":3},{"id":"schemas","text":"Schemas","level":3},{"id":"shared-form-options","text":"Shared form options","level":2},{"id":"form-groups-and-field-groups","text":"Form groups and field groups","level":2},{"id":"listeners","text":"Listeners","level":2},{"id":"server-and-framework-integrations","text":"Server and framework integrations","level":2},{"id":"migration-order-for-an-app","text":"Migration order for an app","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Form v2 keeps the same core idea as v1: create a form with\n`useForm`, render fields from the returned form API, and submit with\n`form.handleSubmit()`. Most migrations are not a full rewrite, but v2 does\nchange several React-facing APIs that show up in examples and integration\ntests.\n\nThis page is a starting checklist for migrating React apps from v1 to v2.\n\n## Quick checklist\n\n- Keep `useForm`, `defaultValues`, `onSubmit`, `form.Field`, and\n  `form.Subscribe`, but update render props from `field.state.value` and\n  `field.state.meta` to `field.value` and `field.meta`.\n- Always provide `defaultValues` to `useForm`. v2 does not support omitting\n  them.\n- Move field-level `defaultValue` props into form-level `defaultValues`.\n- Remove field-level `defaultMeta` props. Model initial validation and error\n  visibility through validators, `runOnMount`, and `errorVisibility`.\n- Change validation from keyed event objects like `{ onChange, onBlur }` to\n  arrays of validator objects with `run` and `triggers`.\n- Change async validator debounce options such as `onChangeAsyncDebounceMs` to\n  `triggerDebounceMs` on the validator object.\n- Change field cross-validation from `onChangeListenTo` / `onBlurListenTo` to\n  `watchFields` on validators or listeners.\n- Replace `mode=\"array\"` fields with `form.ArrayField`.\n- Keep array mutations on the `ArrayField` render prop, such as\n  `array.pushValue(...)`, or use path-based form methods such as\n  `form.pushFieldValue(...)` when the control lives outside the render prop.\n- Rename `form.moveFieldValues` to `form.moveFieldValue`, and replace removed\n  form methods such as `setFieldMeta` and `validateField` as described in\n  [Removed and renamed form methods](#removed-and-renamed-form-methods).\n- Read errors from `field.errors`, `group.state.errors`, and\n  `form.state.errors` as validation issue objects. Use `error.message` when\n  rendering text.\n- In form- and group-level validators, build routed errors with\n  `createErrorMap(...)` and return the map directly.\n- Return `createValidationError(...)` from `onSubmit` when a submit handler\n  needs to route server errors back to form or field state.\n- Use `useSelector`, which replaces v1's deprecated `useStore` usage.\n- Subscribe to `form.atom` and `field.atom` instead of `form.store` and\n  `field.store`.\n- Use `formOptions(...)` for shared base form options.\n- Replace `withForm` components with plain components that accept a `form` prop\n  typed as `ReactFormType<typeof formOpts>`.\n- Replace `useFormGroup` with `form.FormGroup` for scoped sections of the same\n  form.\n- Replace `withFieldGroup` with `defineFieldGroup(...).bindComponent(...)` for\n  reusable field bundles that map virtual field names to different concrete\n  form paths.\n- Upgrade Vue to version 3.6 or newer when using the Vue adapter. Form\n  Composition relies on behavior introduced in Vue 3.6.\n- Update CommonJS integrations to consume ESM. The v2 packages do not publish\n  a CommonJS build and require Node.js 18 or newer.\n- Upgrade React to version 18 or newer. The v2 React adapter no longer supports\n  React 17.\n- Update CommonJS integrations to consume ESM. The v2 packages do not publish\n  a CommonJS build and require Node.js 18 or newer.\n\n## React version\n\nThe v2 React adapter supports React 18 and 19. React 17 is no longer supported,\nso upgrade `react`, `react-dom`, and their corresponding type packages before\nmigrating. If you imported `CrossVersionReactNode` from `@tanstack/react-form`,\nimport `ReactNode` from `react` instead.\n\n## Vue version\n\nThe v2 Vue adapter requires Vue 3.6 or newer. At the time of writing, Vue 3.6\nhas not yet been released as stable and is available as a release candidate.\nWe hope Vue 3.6 will be stable by the time TanStack Form v2 becomes stable.\n\nForm Composition relies on Vue 3.6 behavior to work correctly. Requiring it\nfrom the start lets the Vue adapter support Form Composition without adding a\nbreaking minimum-version change later in the v2 release line.\n\n## Package format\n\nThe v2 core, framework, devtools, and server-adapter packages publish ESM\nexports only and declare Node.js 18 as their minimum version. Prefer `import` /\n`export` syntax, use dynamic `import()` when consuming them from CommonJS, and\nmake sure any Node-based test, SSR, or build tooling can load ESM dependencies.\nThere is no separate CommonJS build or `require` export to fall back to.\n\n## Basic fields\n\nThe v1 simple example and v2 basic example are intentionally similar. The main\nrender-prop difference is that v2 exposes the subscribed field surface directly.\n\n```tsx\n// v1\n<form.Field name=\"firstName\">\n  {(field) => (\n    <input\n      name={field.name}\n      value={field.state.value}\n      onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n      onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n    />\n  )}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\n```tsx\n// v2\n<form.Field name=\"firstName\">\n  {(field) => (\n    <input\n      name={field.name}\n      value={field.value}\n      onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n      onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n      aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\n    />\n  )}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\nThe same applies to common meta and error reads:\n\n```tsx\n// v1\nfield.state.value\nfield.state.meta.isTouched\nfield.state.meta.isValid\nfield.state.meta.errors.join(',')\n```\n\n```tsx\n// v2\nfield.value\nfield.meta.isTouched\nfield.meta.isValid\nfield.errors.map((error) => error.message).join(',')\n```\n\nv2 also exposes `field.meta.isInvalid`, which is the inverse of `isValid` and\nis convenient for attributes such as `aria-invalid`.\n\nThe v2 React integration tests also assert that fields rerender independently\nwhen sibling fields change. Prefer reading only the subscribed field values and\nmeta you need in each render prop.\n\n## Defaults and initial meta\n\nIn v1, a form could rely on field-level `defaultValue` props:\n\n```tsx\n// v1\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {} as Person,\n})\n\n<form.Field name=\"firstName\" defaultValue=\"\">\n  {(field) => <input value={field.state.value} />}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\nIn v2, `defaultValues` are required on the form and are the only place to define\ninitial values:\n\n```tsx\n// v2\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    lastName: '',\n  },\n})\n\n<form.Field name=\"firstName\">\n  {(field) => <input value={field.value} />}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\n`<form.Field defaultMeta={...}>` was also removed. If v1 code used\n`defaultMeta={{ isTouched: true }}` to show errors immediately, replace the\nimplicit meta state with mount validation and an explicit visibility policy:\n\n```tsx\n// v2\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n  },\n})\n\n<form.Field\n  name=\"firstName\"\n  validators={[\n    {\n      runOnMount: true,\n      triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n      run: ({ value }) => (value ? undefined : 'First name is required'),\n    },\n  ]}\n>\n  {(field) => (\n    <>\n      <input\n        value={field.value}\n        onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n        onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n      />\n      {field.errors.map((error) => (\n        <p key={error.message}>{error.message}</p>\n      ))}\n    </>\n  )}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\nIf errors should validate on mount but remain hidden until the user blurs the\nfield or tries to submit, use a form-level policy such as\n`errorVisibility: ({ fieldState, state }) => fieldState.meta.isBlurred ||\nstate.submissionAttempts > 0` instead.\n\n## Validators\n\nv1 validators are keyed by event names:\n\n```tsx\n// v1\n<form.Field\n  name=\"firstName\"\n  validators={{\n    onChange: ({ value }) =>\n      !value\n        ? 'A first name is required'\n        : value.length < 3\n          ? 'First name must be at least 3 characters'\n          : undefined,\n    onChangeAsyncDebounceMs: 500,\n    onChangeAsync: async ({ value }) => {\n      await checkName(value)\n      return value.includes('error')\n        ? 'No \"error\" allowed in first name'\n        : undefined\n    },\n  }}\n/>\n```\n\nv2 validators are ordered arrays. Each validator has a `run` function or\nstandard schema, a `triggers` list, and optional behavior like debouncing or\nbailing:\n\n```tsx\n// v2\n<form.Field\n  name=\"firstName\"\n  validators={[\n    {\n      run: ({ value }) => {\n        if (value.length === 0) return 'A first name is required'\n        if (value.length < 3) return 'First name is too short'\n      },\n      triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n      triggerDebounceMs: 300,\n    },\n    {\n      run: async ({ value }) => {\n        await checkName(value)\n        return value.toLowerCase().includes('error')\n          ? 'No \"error\" allowed in first name'\n          : undefined\n      },\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      bailIfInvalid: true,\n    },\n  ]}\n/>\n```\n\nUseful translations:\n\n| v1                                    | v2                                                                               |\n| ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `validators.onMount`                  | validator with `runOnMount: true`                                                |\n| `validators.onChange`                 | validator with `triggers: ['change']`                                            |\n| `validators.onBlur`                   | validator with `triggers: ['blur']`                                              |\n| `validators.onSubmit`                 | validator with `triggers: []`, or rely on submit running validators by default   |\n| `onChangeAsync`                       | async `run` with `triggers: ['change']`                                          |\n| `onChangeAsyncDebounceMs`             | `triggerDebounceMs`                                                              |\n| `onChangeListenTo` / `onBlurListenTo` | `watchFields`                                                                    |\n| `validationLogic: revalidateLogic()`  | migrate to explicit `triggers`, `when`, `runOnSubmit`, and `bailIfInvalid` rules |\n\nSubmission is separate from the `triggers` list: every validator runs during\nsubmission by default. An empty `triggers: []` therefore means \"no change or\nblur validation, but still validate on submit.\" Set `runOnSubmit: false` when a\nvalidator must not run during client submission; do not add `'submit'` to\n`triggers`.\n\n`triggers` can contain strings or trigger config objects. Use config objects\nwhen a validator should only run for some changes:\n\n```tsx\nvalidators={[\n  {\n    triggers: [\n      {\n        trigger: 'change',\n        when: ({ value }) => Boolean(value),\n      },\n    ],\n    watchFields: ['startDate'],\n    run: ({ value, formApi }) => {\n      const startDate = formApi.getFieldValue('startDate')\n      if (value < startDate) return 'End date must be after the start date'\n    },\n  },\n]}\n```\n\nPredicate callbacks are scope-aware. A `when` callback, a function-valued\n`runOnSubmit`, or a function-valued `triggerDebounceMs` receives `scope` and\n`formApi`; field predicates receive the field being validated as `fieldApi`,\nwhile group predicates also receive `groupApi`. For form and group predicates,\nan optional `fieldApi` is the field that triggered validation.\n\nUse `createValidator(...)` when the scheduling policy should be reused with\ndifferent validator functions or schemas while preserving their inferred\ntypes:\n\n```tsx\nimport { createValidator } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nconst validateAfterSubmit = createValidator({\n  triggers: [\n    {\n      trigger: 'change',\n      when: ({ groupApi, formApi }) =>\n        (groupApi?.state.submissionAttempts ??\n          formApi.state.submissionAttempts) > 0,\n    },\n  ],\n})\n\nconst validators = [validateAfterSubmit(schema)]\n```\n\n## Standard schemas\n\nv1 accepted standard schemas in event-keyed validators:\n\n```tsx\n// v1\nuseForm({\n  defaultValues,\n  validators: {\n    onChange: schema,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nIn v2, pass schemas as `run` values inside the validators array:\n\n```tsx\n// v2\nuseForm({\n  defaultValues,\n  validators: [\n    {\n      run: schema,\n      triggers: ['change'],\n    },\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nThe form's `value` remains its editable input state. When a Standard Schema\nvalidator runs successfully during submission, its parsed output is available\nin `onSubmit` at the corresponding `schemaOutputs` index. Non-schema entries\nare `undefined`. Validators with literal `runOnSubmit: false` are skipped during\nsubmission, and their slots are typed as `undefined`. Use the parsed entry when\nan endpoint expects the schema's output type.\n\nFor schema-led option inference, pass the schema first and the options second.\n`formOptions.strictSchema(...)` uses the schema input as the form shape, while\n`formOptions.looseSchema(...)` permits editable nullish defaults and combines\nthem with the schema shape. These option helpers only affect types; the\nvalidators still perform the runtime parsing.\n\nWhen manually calling a schema, return `parseIssues(...)` with the failed issue\narray. In a field validator it produces field issues; in a form or group\nvalidator it routes issue paths into a form/field map; and in `onSubmit` it\nproduces a branded submit validation result. The v2 field-group example uses\nthis helper after calling `schema.safeParse(...)`.\n\n## Errors and submit results\n\nv1 examples commonly render errors from `field.state.meta.errors`. In v2,\nrender from `field.errors` for fields, `group.state.errors` for form groups, and\n`form.state.errors` for the form. Each of the group and form collections is an\narray. The items are validation issue objects, so render `error.message`.\n\n```tsx\nfunction FieldError({ field }: { field: AnyFieldApi }) {\n  return (\n    <small role={field.meta.isInvalid ? 'alert' : undefined} aria-live=\"polite\">\n      {field.errors.map((error) => error.message).join('\\n')}\n    </small>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nForm- and group-level validators can route errors to the form and individual\nfields. Build a map with the `createErrorMap` supplied to `run`, then return the\nmap itself:\n\n```tsx\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n  },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: ({ value, createErrorMap }) => {\n        const errors = createErrorMap()\n\n        if (!value.firstName.trim()) {\n          errors.form = 'Please correct the highlighted fields'\n          errors.fields.firstName = 'First name is required'\n        }\n\n        return errors\n      },\n    },\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n`createErrorMap` also accepts an initial `{ form, fields }` object. An empty\nreturned map is treated as a valid result.\nField-level validators continue to return their own issue, string, issue array,\nor a valid result directly.\n\nSubmit handlers can now return a typed validation result. Use\n`createValidationError` to route endpoint errors back into form state:\n\n```tsx\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    lastName: '',\n  },\n  onSubmit: async ({ value, createValidationError }) => {\n    const result = await saveUser(value)\n\n    if (!result.ok) {\n      return createValidationError({\n        form: 'Could not save user',\n        fields: {\n          firstName: 'Name already exists',\n          lastName: 'Name already exists',\n        },\n      })\n    }\n\n    return null\n  },\n})\n```\n\n`form.handleSubmit()` resolves to the validation-result array for that\nsubmission attempt, so framework examples can await it and continue to native\nor server submission when `errors.length === 0`. A thrown or rejected\n`onSubmit` marks submission unsuccessful but is not added to that array. Return\n`createValidationError(...)` or `parseIssues(...)` when a submit failure should\nbecome validation state.\n\n## Selectors and atoms\n\nv1 re-exported `useStore` from `@tanstack/react-store`, but that usage was\ndeprecated before v2. In v2, use `useSelector` and subscribe to atoms:\n\n```tsx\n// v1\nimport { useStore } from '@tanstack/react-store'\n\nconst errors = useStore(form.store, (state) => state.errors)\nconst fieldErrors = useStore(field.store, (state) => state.meta.errors)\n```\n\n```tsx\n// v2\nimport { useSelector } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nconst errors = useSelector(form.atom, (state) => state.errors)\nconst fieldErrors = useSelector(field.atom, (state) => state.meta.errors)\n```\n\nThe same rename applies when subscribing to field groups:\n\n```tsx\nconst values = useSelector(fields.atom, (values) => values)\n```\n\nReading `form.state` or `group.state` gives an imperative snapshot; it does not\nsubscribe a React component. Use field render props, `form.Subscribe`,\n`group.Subscribe`, or `useSelector` for reactive reads, and keep selectors\nfocused on the state the component renders.\n\n## Arrays\n\nv1 represented array fields with `mode=\"array\"` and exposed array helpers from\nthe field render prop:\n\n```tsx\n// v1\n<form.Field name=\"people\" mode=\"array\">\n  {(field) => (\n    <>\n      {field.state.value.map((_, index) => (\n        <form.Field key={index} name={`people[${index}].name`}>\n          {(subField) => (\n            <input\n              value={subField.state.value}\n              onChange={(event) => subField.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n            />\n          )}\n        </form.Field>\n      ))}\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        onClick={() => field.pushValue({ name: '', age: 0 })}\n      >\n        Add person\n      </button>\n    </>\n  )}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\nv2 uses a dedicated `form.ArrayField` component for array subscriptions. Its\nrender prop still exposes array methods, so the direct migration can keep the\nmutation next to the rendered array:\n\n```tsx\n// v2\n<form.ArrayField name=\"people\">\n  {(array) => (\n    <>\n      {array.value.map((_, index) => (\n        <form.Field key={index} name={`people[${index}].name`}>\n          {(field) => (\n            <input\n              name={field.name}\n              value={field.value}\n              onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n              onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n            />\n          )}\n        </form.Field>\n      ))}\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        onClick={() => array.pushValue({ name: '', age: 0 })}\n      >\n        Add person\n      </button>\n    </>\n  )}\n</form.ArrayField>\n```\n\nWhen the mutation control is outside `ArrayField`, use the path-based form API\ninstead:\n\n```tsx\nform.pushFieldValue('people', { name: '', age: 0 })\n```\n\nThe same choice is available for inserting, removing, moving, swapping,\nfiltering, and clearing values: use the relative methods on `array` or the\nfield-path methods on `form`.\n\nThe v2 array example calls out the performance reason for this change:\n`ArrayField` lets the array shell rerender when the array structure changes\nwithout forcing the whole list to rerender for every item value change.\n\nFor current usage and adapter-specific examples, see [Arrays](./arrays).\n\n## Removed and renamed form methods\n\nThe v2 form API is smaller than v1's. It reads and updates values, mutates\narrays, runs form-level validation, submits, and resets. Field metadata now\nlives on the field API, validators and submit results produce errors instead\nof code writing them directly, and nothing replaces the internal\nfield-registry helpers.\n\n| v1                                                      | v2                                                                                                 |\n| ------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `moveFieldValues(name, from, to)`                       | `moveFieldValue(name, from, to)`                                                                   |\n| `setFieldMeta(name, updater)`                           | `setFieldValue` update options, `handleSubmit()`, or `errorVisibility`                             |\n| `getFieldMeta(name)`                                    | `field.meta`                                                                                       |\n| `resetFieldMeta(...)`                                   | `resetField(name)`, `field.reset()`, or `reset(form.state.values, { updateDefaultValues: false })` |\n| `validateField(name, cause)`                            | validator `triggers` and `watchFields`                                                             |\n| `validateAllFields(cause)`                              | `handleSubmit()`                                                                                   |\n| `validateArrayFieldsStartingFrom(...)`                  | array methods run change validation unless `causeValidation: false`                                |\n| `validate(cause)`                                       | `validate('change' \\| 'blur')`, which runs form-level validators only                              |\n| `getAllErrors()`                                        | `form.state.errors`, `field.errors`, `form.state.isValid`, or the `handleSubmit()` result          |\n| `setErrorMap(errorMap)`                                 | errors returned from validators, `createValidationError(...)` from `onSubmit`, or `serverState`    |\n| `deleteField(name)`                                     | `removeFieldValue` / `filterFieldValues` for array items, `setFieldValue` on the parent object     |\n| `getFieldInfo(name)`                                    | none; it exposed internal field registration                                                       |\n| `parseValuesWithSchema(schema)` and its `Async` variant | a schema validator plus `schemaOutputs` in `onSubmit`, or call the schema directly                 |\n| `getFormGroupMeta(name)`                                | `group.state` from `form.FormGroup`                                                                |\n\n### Field metadata\n\nv1 code often wrote field meta directly, for example to mark a field as touched\nwhen its value was set programmatically. In v2, meta is derived from updates.\nPass `FieldUpdateOptions` to `setFieldValue`, the array methods, or\n`field.handleChange` to control what an update marks:\n\n```tsx\n// v1\nform.setFieldValue('firstName', 'Ada', {\n  dontUpdateMeta: true,\n  dontValidate: true,\n})\nform.setFieldMeta('firstName', (prev) => ({ ...prev, isTouched: true }))\n```\n\n```tsx\n// v2\nform.setFieldValue('firstName', 'Ada', {\n  markAsTouched: true,\n  markAsDirty: false,\n  causeValidation: false,\n})\n```\n\n| v1 update option   | v2 update option                             |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `dontUpdateMeta`   | `markAsTouched: false`, `markAsDirty: false` |\n| `dontValidate`     | `causeValidation: false`                     |\n| `dontRunListeners` | none                                         |\n\nTo touch every field before showing errors, call `form.handleSubmit()`, which\nmarks all registered fields as touched. To show errors without touching fields,\nconfigure `errorVisibility` instead.\n\nRead meta from the field API, as `field.meta` in a render prop or with\n`useSelector(field.atom, (state) => state.meta)`. The form API does not look up\nmeta by path.\n\nTo clear meta, `form.resetField(name)` and `field.reset()` reset one field's\nvalue and meta. To clear every field's meta but keep the values the user\nentered, reset the form to its current values without moving the default\nbaseline:\n\n```tsx\nform.reset(form.state.values, { updateDefaultValues: false })\n```\n\nThis also clears form-level errors, submission state, and dirty history.\n\n### On-demand validation\n\nv2 has no public method that validates a single field or every field outside\nsubmission. Express when a field validates through its validators instead:\n\n- Use `triggers` to choose the events that run a validator.\n- Use `watchFields` to rerun a validator when another field changes, which\n  covers most v1 `validateField` calls made from another field's `onChange`.\n- Call `form.handleSubmit()` to validate every field and the form together.\n  Unlike `validateAllFields`, it also calls `onSubmit` when validation passes.\n  It resolves to the error results, so an empty array means everything is\n  valid.\n\n`form.validate('change')` and `form.validate('blur')` still exist, but they run\nform-level validators only. Field validators do not run.\n\n### Errors\n\nv2 does not write error maps directly. Return errors from a validator, or from\n`onSubmit` with `createValidationError(...)` as shown in\n[Errors and submit results](#errors-and-submit-results). For server-rendered\nerrors, pass `serverState` to `useForm`.\n\nTo read errors, `form.state.errors` holds form-level errors only. Errors routed\nto fields stay on the fields, available as `field.errors`. Use\n`form.state.isValid` to check both levels at once.\n\n### Schemas\n\n`parseValuesWithSchema` checked the current values against a schema without\nstoring errors. To keep that behavior, call the schema yourself:\n\n```tsx\nconst result = await schema['~standard'].validate(form.state.values)\n\nif (result.issues) {\n  // handle issues\n}\n```\n\nTo validate with the schema and use its parsed output, add it to `validators`\nand read `schemaOutputs` in `onSubmit`, as described in\n[Standard schemas](#standard-schemas).\n\n## Shared form options\n\nFor extracted components, v1 composition examples often use a custom\n`useAppForm` hook plus `withForm` from `createFormHook`. v2 still supports app\nform hooks, but `withForm` was removed. The smaller building block for shared\ndefaults is `formOptions(...)`:\n\n```tsx\nimport { formOptions } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nexport const sharedFormOptions = formOptions({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    lastName: '',\n    address: {\n      street: '',\n      country: '',\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nconst form = useForm({\n  ...sharedFormOptions,\n  onSubmit: ({ value }) => {\n    console.log(value)\n  },\n})\n```\n\nWhen typing extracted components, prefer the v2 public types covered in\n[Splitting forms](./splitting-forms):\n\n```tsx\nimport type { AnyReactFormApi, FieldWithValue } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nfunction StringField({ field }: { field: FieldWithValue<string> }) {\n  return (\n    <input\n      value={field.value}\n      onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n    />\n  )\n}\n\nfunction SubmitButton({ form }: { form: AnyReactFormApi }) {\n  return (\n    <form.Subscribe selector={(state) => [state.canSubmit, state.isSubmitting]}>\n      {([canSubmit, isSubmitting]) => (\n        <button type=\"submit\" disabled={!canSubmit || isSubmitting}>\n          {isSubmitting ? '...' : 'Submit'}\n        </button>\n      )}\n    </form.Subscribe>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n`AnyReactFormApi` and `FieldWithValue<T>` intentionally erase unrelated type\ndetails for generic UI pieces. Use `ReactFormType<typeof formOpts>` when a\ncomponent needs the option-derived data and field-path surface. Options created\nwith `appFormOptions` also retain their app component map. Submit error types\nmay intentionally widen when the shared options omit `onSubmit` so it can be\nsupplied later. Prefer these aliases over spelling the full `FormApi` or\n`FieldApi` generic lists in application components.\n\nFor components that previously used `withForm`, pass the form API explicitly and\ntype it from the same options object:\n\n```tsx\n// v1\nconst AddressFields = withForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    address: {\n      street: '',\n      country: '',\n    },\n  },\n  render: ({ form }) => (\n    <>\n      <form.Field name=\"address.street\">{/* ... */}</form.Field>\n      <form.Field name=\"address.country\">{/* ... */}</form.Field>\n    </>\n  ),\n})\n```\n\n```tsx\n// v2\nimport { formOptions } from '@tanstack/react-form'\nimport type { ReactFormType } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nexport const profileFormOptions = formOptions({\n  defaultValues: {\n    address: {\n      street: '',\n      country: '',\n    },\n  },\n})\n\ninterface AddressFieldsProps {\n  form: ReactFormType<typeof profileFormOptions>\n}\n\nfunction AddressFields({ form }: AddressFieldsProps) {\n  return (\n    <>\n      <form.Field name=\"address.street\">{/* ... */}</form.Field>\n      <form.Field name=\"address.country\">{/* ... */}</form.Field>\n    </>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Form groups and field groups\n\nReplace v1 form group usage with `form.FormGroup`. It is the v2 tool for\nmulti-step forms and scoped validation when a section is part of one concrete\nform shape:\n\n```tsx\n<form.FormGroup name=\"guestDetails\" onSubmit={() => goToNextStep()}>\n  {(group) => (\n    <>\n      <group.Field name=\"name\">\n        {(field) => (\n          <input\n            value={field.value}\n            onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n          />\n        )}\n      </group.Field>\n      <button type=\"button\" onClick={() => group.handleSubmit()}>\n        Continue\n      </button>\n    </>\n  )}\n</form.FormGroup>\n```\n\nInside the group, field names are scoped. `name=\"name\"` becomes\n`guestDetails.name`, `group.ArrayField name=\"guests\"` becomes\n`guestDetails.guests`, and watched fields are scoped the same way.\n\nGroup submission is its own validation cycle. `group.handleSubmit()` validates\nthe group and its fields and then calls the group's `onSubmit` or\n`onSubmitInvalid`; `form.handleSubmit()` does not also run the group's\nvalidators. Keep any rules required for final whole-form submission in the\nform-level validator pipeline as well. `group.handleSubmit()` resolves to an\nerror array, and `group.state.errors` is an array.\n\nFor a field inside a mounted group, scalar state exposed to `errorVisibility`\n(such as `submissionAttempts` and `isDirty`) is scoped to the nearest group.\nThe callback's `values` and `errors` remain form-wide.\n\nv1's `withFieldGroup` HOC was removed. v2 replaces it with\n`defineFieldGroup(...)` for reusable field bundles. Use it when a component\nshould not care where its fields live in the parent form:\n\n```tsx\nimport { defineFieldGroup } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nconst rangeFieldGroup = defineFieldGroup(({ strict }) => ({\n  lower: strict<string>(),\n  upper: strict<string>(),\n}))\n\nfunction RangeFieldsImpl({\n  fields,\n}: {\n  fields: typeof rangeFieldGroup.fields\n}) {\n  return (\n    <>\n      <fields.Field name=\"lower\">\n        {(field) => (\n          <input\n            value={field.value}\n            onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n          />\n        )}\n      </fields.Field>\n      <fields.Field\n        name=\"upper\"\n        validators={[\n          {\n            triggers: ['change'],\n            watchFields: ['lower'],\n            run: ({ value }) => {\n              const lower = fields.getFieldValue('lower')\n              if (Number(value) < Number(lower)) {\n                return 'Upper bound must be greater than lower bound'\n              }\n            },\n          },\n        ]}\n      >\n        {(field) => (\n          <input\n            value={field.value}\n            onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n          />\n        )}\n      </fields.Field>\n    </>\n  )\n}\n\nexport const RangeFields = rangeFieldGroup.bindComponent(\n  RangeFieldsImpl,\n  'fields',\n)\n```\n\nThen bind virtual names to concrete paths wherever the group is used:\n\n```tsx\n<RangeFields\n  form={form}\n  fields={{\n    lower: 'minPrice',\n    upper: 'maxPrice',\n  }}\n/>\n```\n\nUse this v2 pattern to migrate v1 `withFieldGroup` components that were reused\nagainst different field paths. If you are using app form components from\n`createFormHook`, wrap components that expect an injected field API with\n`getFormHookHelpers()`, then define field groups with `defineAppFieldGroup`:\n\n```tsx\nimport { createFormHook, getFormHookHelpers } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nconst { fieldComponent } = getFormHookHelpers()\nconst AppTextField = fieldComponent.strict(StringField, 'field')\n\nconst { appFormOptions, useAppForm, defineAppFieldGroup } = createFormHook({\n  fieldComponents: {\n    TextField: AppTextField,\n  },\n  formComponents: {},\n})\n\nconst contactFieldGroup = defineAppFieldGroup(({ strict }) => ({\n  name: strict<string>(),\n}))\n```\n\n## Listeners\n\nv1 listeners were event-keyed objects. v2 listeners use a validator-like array\nshape with `run`, `triggers`, and optional `triggerDebounceMs`. A trigger can be\na string or `{ trigger, when }`, and debounce can be a number or a callback.\nForm listeners support `change`, `blur`, `submit`, `mount`, and `reset`; field\nlisteners additionally support `unmount`.\n\n```tsx\n// v2\n<form.Field\n  name=\"amount\"\n  listeners={[\n    {\n      triggers: ['blur'],\n      run: ({ value, fieldApi }) => {\n        fieldApi.handleChange(Number(value).toFixed(2))\n      },\n    },\n  ]}\n/>\n```\n\nFor cross-field field listeners, put the source fields in `watchFields`. In\n`form.FormGroup` and field-group-bound components, `watchFields` uses the scoped\nor virtual field names and v2 resolves them to the concrete form paths.\nForm-level listeners instead observe propagated events and receive an optional\nsource field as `triggerFieldApi`. It is present for propagated field changes\nand blurs, but absent for form-originated events such as mount, reset, and\nsubmit.\n\n## Server and framework integrations\n\nThe v1 examples include Next server actions, Remix, and TanStack Start examples\nthat use v1's keyed validators and store-level errors. The v2 examples show a\nnew server-validation model in `@tanstack/react-form-start` and a Next.js\nexample with shared isomorphic validation.\n\nKey changes:\n\n- Import `serverValidateHelper` from `@tanstack/react-form`, then import the\n  framework adapter from `@tanstack/react-form-start`,\n  `@tanstack/react-form-nextjs`.\n- Share common form configuration with `formOptions(...)`.\n- Return the `createErrorMap()` map directly from framework/server validators\n  when routing form and field errors.\n- Combine `triggers: ['server']` with `runOnSubmit: false` for a form validator\n  that must run only on the server. Server-triggered validators otherwise still\n  run during client submission because submission is enabled by default.\n- Next.js and Remix adapters, and the Start adapter when no callback override is\n  supplied, resolve to\n  `{ success: true, values, schemaOutputs }` or\n  `{ success: false, serverState }`. Pass the failure's `serverState` back to\n  `useForm({ ...formOpts, serverState })` on the client.\n- `@tanstack/react-form-remix` was removed.\n\nFor example, a Start adapter is configured separately from the shared form\noptions:\n\n```tsx\nimport { serverValidateHelper } from '@tanstack/react-form'\nimport { start } from '@tanstack/react-form-start'\n\nconst { createServerValidate } = serverValidateHelper({\n  framework: start(),\n})\n\nconst serverValidate = createServerValidate(formOpts)\n```\n\nIn `formOpts`, a server-only validator returns its routed error map directly:\n\n```tsx\n{\n  triggers: ['server'],\n  runOnSubmit: false,\n  run: ({ value, createErrorMap }) => {\n    const errors = createErrorMap()\n\n    if (value.age < 13) {\n      errors.fields.age = 'You must be at least 13'\n    }\n\n    return errors\n  },\n}\n```\n\nClient rendering still follows the same v2 field surface:\n\n```tsx\n<form.Field name=\"age\">\n  {(field) => (\n    <>\n      <input\n        name={field.name}\n        value={field.value}\n        onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n        onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(Number(event.target.value))}\n      />\n      {field.errors.map((error) => (\n        <div key={error.message} role=\"alert\">\n          {error.message}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </>\n  )}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\n## Migration order for an app\n\n1. Upgrade imports and keep the smallest possible form compiling with\n   ESM `import` syntax, `useForm`, `defaultValues`, `form.Field`, and\n   `form.handleSubmit()`.\n2. Move every field-level `defaultValue` into form-level `defaultValues` and\n   remove `defaultMeta`.\n3. Update field render props from `field.state.*` to the direct v2 surface.\n4. Replace `useStore(...store...)` with `useSelector(...atom...)`.\n5. Convert validators and listeners to arrays, paying special attention to the\n   default submit behavior.\n6. Convert arrays from `mode=\"array\"` to `form.ArrayField`; keep relative\n   mutators on its render prop or move them to path-based form methods.\n7. Return `createErrorMap(...)` directly from form, group, and server validators,\n   and convert submitted endpoint errors to `createValidationError(...)`.\n8. Revisit composition: use `formOptions(...)` for shared options,\n   `ReactFormType<typeof formOpts>` for extracted form props,\n   `form.FormGroup` for scoped sections, and\n   `defineFieldGroup(...).bindComponent(...)` for reusable field bundles.\n9. Re-run React integration tests around validation timing, field rerenders,\n   groups, server error hydration, and array mutations. These are the areas\n   where v2 intentionally tightened behavior.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: migrate-from-v1\ntitle: Migrating from v1\n---\n\nTanStack Form v2 keeps the same core idea as v1: create a form with\n`useForm`, render fields from the returned form API, and submit with\n`form.handleSubmit()`. Most migrations are not a full rewrite, but v2 does\nchange several React-facing APIs that show up in examples and integration\ntests.\n\nThis page is a starting checklist for migrating React apps from v1 to v2.\n\n## Quick checklist\n\n- Keep `useForm`, `defaultValues`, `onSubmit`, `form.Field`, and\n  `form.Subscribe`, but update render props from `field.state.value` and\n  `field.state.meta` to `field.value` and `field.meta`.\n- Always provide `defaultValues` to `useForm`. v2 does not support omitting\n  them.\n- Move field-level `defaultValue` props into form-level `defaultValues`.\n- Remove field-level `defaultMeta` props. Model initial validation and error\n  visibility through validators, `runOnMount`, and `errorVisibility`.\n- Change validation from keyed event objects like `{ onChange, onBlur }` to\n  arrays of validator objects with `run` and `triggers`.\n- Change async validator debounce options such as `onChangeAsyncDebounceMs` to\n  `triggerDebounceMs` on the validator object.\n- Change field cross-validation from `onChangeListenTo` / `onBlurListenTo` to\n  `watchFields` on validators or listeners.\n- Replace `mode=\"array\"` fields with `form.ArrayField`.\n- Keep array mutations on the `ArrayField` render prop, such as\n  `array.pushValue(...)`, or use path-based form methods such as\n  `form.pushFieldValue(...)` when the control lives outside the render prop.\n- Rename `form.moveFieldValues` to `form.moveFieldValue`, and replace removed\n  form methods such as `setFieldMeta` and `validateField` as described in\n  [Removed and renamed form methods](#removed-and-renamed-form-methods).\n- Read errors from `field.errors`, `group.state.errors`, and\n  `form.state.errors` as validation issue objects. Use `error.message` when\n  rendering text.\n- In form- and group-level validators, build routed errors with\n  `createErrorMap(...)` and return the map directly.\n- Return `createValidationError(...)` from `onSubmit` when a submit handler\n  needs to route server errors back to form or field state.\n- Use `useSelector`, which replaces v1's deprecated `useStore` usage.\n- Subscribe to `form.atom` and `field.atom` instead of `form.store` and\n  `field.store`.\n- Use `formOptions(...)` for shared base form options.\n- Replace `withForm` components with plain components that accept a `form` prop\n  typed as `ReactFormType<typeof formOpts>`.\n- Replace `useFormGroup` with `form.FormGroup` for scoped sections of the same\n  form.\n- Replace `withFieldGroup` with `defineFieldGroup(...).bindComponent(...)` for\n  reusable field bundles that map virtual field names to different concrete\n  form paths.\n- Upgrade Vue to version 3.6 or newer when using the Vue adapter. Form\n  Composition relies on behavior introduced in Vue 3.6.\n- Update CommonJS integrations to consume ESM. The v2 packages do not publish\n  a CommonJS build and require Node.js 18 or newer.\n- Upgrade React to version 18 or newer. The v2 React adapter no longer supports\n  React 17.\n- Update CommonJS integrations to consume ESM. The v2 packages do not publish\n  a CommonJS build and require Node.js 18 or newer.\n\n## React version\n\nThe v2 React adapter supports React 18 and 19. React 17 is no longer supported,\nso upgrade `react`, `react-dom`, and their corresponding type packages before\nmigrating. If you imported `CrossVersionReactNode` from `@tanstack/react-form`,\nimport `ReactNode` from `react` instead.\n\n## Vue version\n\nThe v2 Vue adapter requires Vue 3.6 or newer. At the time of writing, Vue 3.6\nhas not yet been released as stable and is available as a release candidate.\nWe hope Vue 3.6 will be stable by the time TanStack Form v2 becomes stable.\n\nForm Composition relies on Vue 3.6 behavior to work correctly. Requiring it\nfrom the start lets the Vue adapter support Form Composition without adding a\nbreaking minimum-version change later in the v2 release line.\n\n## Package format\n\nThe v2 core, framework, devtools, and server-adapter packages publish ESM\nexports only and declare Node.js 18 as their minimum version. Prefer `import` /\n`export` syntax, use dynamic `import()` when consuming them from CommonJS, and\nmake sure any Node-based test, SSR, or build tooling can load ESM dependencies.\nThere is no separate CommonJS build or `require` export to fall back to.\n\n## Basic fields\n\nThe v1 simple example and v2 basic example are intentionally similar. The main\nrender-prop difference is that v2 exposes the subscribed field surface directly.\n\n```tsx\n// v1\n<form.Field name=\"firstName\">\n  {(field) => (\n    <input\n      name={field.name}\n      value={field.state.value}\n      onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n      onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n    />\n  )}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\n```tsx\n// v2\n<form.Field name=\"firstName\">\n  {(field) => (\n    <input\n      name={field.name}\n      value={field.value}\n      onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n      onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n      aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\n    />\n  )}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\nThe same applies to common meta and error reads:\n\n```tsx\n// v1\nfield.state.value\nfield.state.meta.isTouched\nfield.state.meta.isValid\nfield.state.meta.errors.join(',')\n```\n\n```tsx\n// v2\nfield.value\nfield.meta.isTouched\nfield.meta.isValid\nfield.errors.map((error) => error.message).join(',')\n```\n\nv2 also exposes `field.meta.isInvalid`, which is the inverse of `isValid` and\nis convenient for attributes such as `aria-invalid`.\n\nThe v2 React integration tests also assert that fields rerender independently\nwhen sibling fields change. Prefer reading only the subscribed field values and\nmeta you need in each render prop.\n\n## Defaults and initial meta\n\nIn v1, a form could rely on field-level `defaultValue` props:\n\n```tsx\n// v1\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {} as Person,\n})\n\n<form.Field name=\"firstName\" defaultValue=\"\">\n  {(field) => <input value={field.state.value} />}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\nIn v2, `defaultValues` are required on the form and are the only place to define\ninitial values:\n\n```tsx\n// v2\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    lastName: '',\n  },\n})\n\n<form.Field name=\"firstName\">\n  {(field) => <input value={field.value} />}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\n`<form.Field defaultMeta={...}>` was also removed. If v1 code used\n`defaultMeta={{ isTouched: true }}` to show errors immediately, replace the\nimplicit meta state with mount validation and an explicit visibility policy:\n\n```tsx\n// v2\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n  },\n})\n\n<form.Field\n  name=\"firstName\"\n  validators={[\n    {\n      runOnMount: true,\n      triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n      run: ({ value }) => (value ? undefined : 'First name is required'),\n    },\n  ]}\n>\n  {(field) => (\n    <>\n      <input\n        value={field.value}\n        onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n        onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n      />\n      {field.errors.map((error) => (\n        <p key={error.message}>{error.message}</p>\n      ))}\n    </>\n  )}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\nIf errors should validate on mount but remain hidden until the user blurs the\nfield or tries to submit, use a form-level policy such as\n`errorVisibility: ({ fieldState, state }) => fieldState.meta.isBlurred ||\nstate.submissionAttempts > 0` instead.\n\n## Validators\n\nv1 validators are keyed by event names:\n\n```tsx\n// v1\n<form.Field\n  name=\"firstName\"\n  validators={{\n    onChange: ({ value }) =>\n      !value\n        ? 'A first name is required'\n        : value.length < 3\n          ? 'First name must be at least 3 characters'\n          : undefined,\n    onChangeAsyncDebounceMs: 500,\n    onChangeAsync: async ({ value }) => {\n      await checkName(value)\n      return value.includes('error')\n        ? 'No \"error\" allowed in first name'\n        : undefined\n    },\n  }}\n/>\n```\n\nv2 validators are ordered arrays. Each validator has a `run` function or\nstandard schema, a `triggers` list, and optional behavior like debouncing or\nbailing:\n\n```tsx\n// v2\n<form.Field\n  name=\"firstName\"\n  validators={[\n    {\n      run: ({ value }) => {\n        if (value.length === 0) return 'A first name is required'\n        if (value.length < 3) return 'First name is too short'\n      },\n      triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n      triggerDebounceMs: 300,\n    },\n    {\n      run: async ({ value }) => {\n        await checkName(value)\n        return value.toLowerCase().includes('error')\n          ? 'No \"error\" allowed in first name'\n          : undefined\n      },\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      bailIfInvalid: true,\n    },\n  ]}\n/>\n```\n\nUseful translations:\n\n| v1                                    | v2                                                                               |\n| ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `validators.onMount`                  | validator with `runOnMount: true`                                                |\n| `validators.onChange`                 | validator with `triggers: ['change']`                                            |\n| `validators.onBlur`                   | validator with `triggers: ['blur']`                                              |\n| `validators.onSubmit`                 | validator with `triggers: []`, or rely on submit running validators by default   |\n| `onChangeAsync`                       | async `run` with `triggers: ['change']`                                          |\n| `onChangeAsyncDebounceMs`             | `triggerDebounceMs`                                                              |\n| `onChangeListenTo` / `onBlurListenTo` | `watchFields`                                                                    |\n| `validationLogic: revalidateLogic()`  | migrate to explicit `triggers`, `when`, `runOnSubmit`, and `bailIfInvalid` rules |\n\nSubmission is separate from the `triggers` list: every validator runs during\nsubmission by default. An empty `triggers: []` therefore means \"no change or\nblur validation, but still validate on submit.\" Set `runOnSubmit: false` when a\nvalidator must not run during client submission; do not add `'submit'` to\n`triggers`.\n\n`triggers` can contain strings or trigger config objects. Use config objects\nwhen a validator should only run for some changes:\n\n```tsx\nvalidators={[\n  {\n    triggers: [\n      {\n        trigger: 'change',\n        when: ({ value }) => Boolean(value),\n      },\n    ],\n    watchFields: ['startDate'],\n    run: ({ value, formApi }) => {\n      const startDate = formApi.getFieldValue('startDate')\n      if (value < startDate) return 'End date must be after the start date'\n    },\n  },\n]}\n```\n\nPredicate callbacks are scope-aware. A `when` callback, a function-valued\n`runOnSubmit`, or a function-valued `triggerDebounceMs` receives `scope` and\n`formApi`; field predicates receive the field being validated as `fieldApi`,\nwhile group predicates also receive `groupApi`. For form and group predicates,\nan optional `fieldApi` is the field that triggered validation.\n\nUse `createValidator(...)` when the scheduling policy should be reused with\ndifferent validator functions or schemas while preserving their inferred\ntypes:\n\n```tsx\nimport { createValidator } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nconst validateAfterSubmit = createValidator({\n  triggers: [\n    {\n      trigger: 'change',\n      when: ({ groupApi, formApi }) =>\n        (groupApi?.state.submissionAttempts ??\n          formApi.state.submissionAttempts) > 0,\n    },\n  ],\n})\n\nconst validators = [validateAfterSubmit(schema)]\n```\n\n## Standard schemas\n\nv1 accepted standard schemas in event-keyed validators:\n\n```tsx\n// v1\nuseForm({\n  defaultValues,\n  validators: {\n    onChange: schema,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nIn v2, pass schemas as `run` values inside the validators array:\n\n```tsx\n// v2\nuseForm({\n  defaultValues,\n  validators: [\n    {\n      run: schema,\n      triggers: ['change'],\n    },\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nThe form's `value` remains its editable input state. When a Standard Schema\nvalidator runs successfully during submission, its parsed output is available\nin `onSubmit` at the corresponding `schemaOutputs` index. Non-schema entries\nare `undefined`. Validators with literal `runOnSubmit: false` are skipped during\nsubmission, and their slots are typed as `undefined`. Use the parsed entry when\nan endpoint expects the schema's output type.\n\nFor schema-led option inference, pass the schema first and the options second.\n`formOptions.strictSchema(...)` uses the schema input as the form shape, while\n`formOptions.looseSchema(...)` permits editable nullish defaults and combines\nthem with the schema shape. These option helpers only affect types; the\nvalidators still perform the runtime parsing.\n\nWhen manually calling a schema, return `parseIssues(...)` with the failed issue\narray. In a field validator it produces field issues; in a form or group\nvalidator it routes issue paths into a form/field map; and in `onSubmit` it\nproduces a branded submit validation result. The v2 field-group example uses\nthis helper after calling `schema.safeParse(...)`.\n\n## Errors and submit results\n\nv1 examples commonly render errors from `field.state.meta.errors`. In v2,\nrender from `field.errors` for fields, `group.state.errors` for form groups, and\n`form.state.errors` for the form. Each of the group and form collections is an\narray. The items are validation issue objects, so render `error.message`.\n\n```tsx\nfunction FieldError({ field }: { field: AnyFieldApi }) {\n  return (\n    <small role={field.meta.isInvalid ? 'alert' : undefined} aria-live=\"polite\">\n      {field.errors.map((error) => error.message).join('\\n')}\n    </small>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nForm- and group-level validators can route errors to the form and individual\nfields. Build a map with the `createErrorMap` supplied to `run`, then return the\nmap itself:\n\n```tsx\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n  },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: ({ value, createErrorMap }) => {\n        const errors = createErrorMap()\n\n        if (!value.firstName.trim()) {\n          errors.form = 'Please correct the highlighted fields'\n          errors.fields.firstName = 'First name is required'\n        }\n\n        return errors\n      },\n    },\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n`createErrorMap` also accepts an initial `{ form, fields }` object. An empty\nreturned map is treated as a valid result.\nField-level validators continue to return their own issue, string, issue array,\nor a valid result directly.\n\nSubmit handlers can now return a typed validation result. Use\n`createValidationError` to route endpoint errors back into form state:\n\n```tsx\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    lastName: '',\n  },\n  onSubmit: async ({ value, createValidationError }) => {\n    const result = await saveUser(value)\n\n    if (!result.ok) {\n      return createValidationError({\n        form: 'Could not save user',\n        fields: {\n          firstName: 'Name already exists',\n          lastName: 'Name already exists',\n        },\n      })\n    }\n\n    return null\n  },\n})\n```\n\n`form.handleSubmit()` resolves to the validation-result array for that\nsubmission attempt, so framework examples can await it and continue to native\nor server submission when `errors.length === 0`. A thrown or rejected\n`onSubmit` marks submission unsuccessful but is not added to that array. Return\n`createValidationError(...)` or `parseIssues(...)` when a submit failure should\nbecome validation state.\n\n## Selectors and atoms\n\nv1 re-exported `useStore` from `@tanstack/react-store`, but that usage was\ndeprecated before v2. In v2, use `useSelector` and subscribe to atoms:\n\n```tsx\n// v1\nimport { useStore } from '@tanstack/react-store'\n\nconst errors = useStore(form.store, (state) => state.errors)\nconst fieldErrors = useStore(field.store, (state) => state.meta.errors)\n```\n\n```tsx\n// v2\nimport { useSelector } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nconst errors = useSelector(form.atom, (state) => state.errors)\nconst fieldErrors = useSelector(field.atom, (state) => state.meta.errors)\n```\n\nThe same rename applies when subscribing to field groups:\n\n```tsx\nconst values = useSelector(fields.atom, (values) => values)\n```\n\nReading `form.state` or `group.state` gives an imperative snapshot; it does not\nsubscribe a React component. Use field render props, `form.Subscribe`,\n`group.Subscribe`, or `useSelector` for reactive reads, and keep selectors\nfocused on the state the component renders.\n\n## Arrays\n\nv1 represented array fields with `mode=\"array\"` and exposed array helpers from\nthe field render prop:\n\n```tsx\n// v1\n<form.Field name=\"people\" mode=\"array\">\n  {(field) => (\n    <>\n      {field.state.value.map((_, index) => (\n        <form.Field key={index} name={`people[${index}].name`}>\n          {(subField) => (\n            <input\n              value={subField.state.value}\n              onChange={(event) => subField.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n            />\n          )}\n        </form.Field>\n      ))}\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        onClick={() => field.pushValue({ name: '', age: 0 })}\n      >\n        Add person\n      </button>\n    </>\n  )}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\nv2 uses a dedicated `form.ArrayField` component for array subscriptions. Its\nrender prop still exposes array methods, so the direct migration can keep the\nmutation next to the rendered array:\n\n```tsx\n// v2\n<form.ArrayField name=\"people\">\n  {(array) => (\n    <>\n      {array.value.map((_, index) => (\n        <form.Field key={index} name={`people[${index}].name`}>\n          {(field) => (\n            <input\n              name={field.name}\n              value={field.value}\n              onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n              onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n            />\n          )}\n        </form.Field>\n      ))}\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        onClick={() => array.pushValue({ name: '', age: 0 })}\n      >\n        Add person\n      </button>\n    </>\n  )}\n</form.ArrayField>\n```\n\nWhen the mutation control is outside `ArrayField`, use the path-based form API\ninstead:\n\n```tsx\nform.pushFieldValue('people', { name: '', age: 0 })\n```\n\nThe same choice is available for inserting, removing, moving, swapping,\nfiltering, and clearing values: use the relative methods on `array` or the\nfield-path methods on `form`.\n\nThe v2 array example calls out the performance reason for this change:\n`ArrayField` lets the array shell rerender when the array structure changes\nwithout forcing the whole list to rerender for every item value change.\n\nFor current usage and adapter-specific examples, see [Arrays](./arrays).\n\n## Removed and renamed form methods\n\nThe v2 form API is smaller than v1's. It reads and updates values, mutates\narrays, runs form-level validation, submits, and resets. Field metadata now\nlives on the field API, validators and submit results produce errors instead\nof code writing them directly, and nothing replaces the internal\nfield-registry helpers.\n\n| v1                                                      | v2                                                                                                 |\n| ------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `moveFieldValues(name, from, to)`                       | `moveFieldValue(name, from, to)`                                                                   |\n| `setFieldMeta(name, updater)`                           | `setFieldValue` update options, `handleSubmit()`, or `errorVisibility`                             |\n| `getFieldMeta(name)`                                    | `field.meta`                                                                                       |\n| `resetFieldMeta(...)`                                   | `resetField(name)`, `field.reset()`, or `reset(form.state.values, { updateDefaultValues: false })` |\n| `validateField(name, cause)`                            | validator `triggers` and `watchFields`                                                             |\n| `validateAllFields(cause)`                              | `handleSubmit()`                                                                                   |\n| `validateArrayFieldsStartingFrom(...)`                  | array methods run change validation unless `causeValidation: false`                                |\n| `validate(cause)`                                       | `validate('change' \\| 'blur')`, which runs form-level validators only                              |\n| `getAllErrors()`                                        | `form.state.errors`, `field.errors`, `form.state.isValid`, or the `handleSubmit()` result          |\n| `setErrorMap(errorMap)`                                 | errors returned from validators, `createValidationError(...)` from `onSubmit`, or `serverState`    |\n| `deleteField(name)`                                     | `removeFieldValue` / `filterFieldValues` for array items, `setFieldValue` on the parent object     |\n| `getFieldInfo(name)`                                    | none; it exposed internal field registration                                                       |\n| `parseValuesWithSchema(schema)` and its `Async` variant | a schema validator plus `schemaOutputs` in `onSubmit`, or call the schema directly                 |\n| `getFormGroupMeta(name)`                                | `group.state` from `form.FormGroup`                                                                |\n\n### Field metadata\n\nv1 code often wrote field meta directly, for example to mark a field as touched\nwhen its value was set programmatically. In v2, meta is derived from updates.\nPass `FieldUpdateOptions` to `setFieldValue`, the array methods, or\n`field.handleChange` to control what an update marks:\n\n```tsx\n// v1\nform.setFieldValue('firstName', 'Ada', {\n  dontUpdateMeta: true,\n  dontValidate: true,\n})\nform.setFieldMeta('firstName', (prev) => ({ ...prev, isTouched: true }))\n```\n\n```tsx\n// v2\nform.setFieldValue('firstName', 'Ada', {\n  markAsTouched: true,\n  markAsDirty: false,\n  causeValidation: false,\n})\n```\n\n| v1 update option   | v2 update option                             |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `dontUpdateMeta`   | `markAsTouched: false`, `markAsDirty: false` |\n| `dontValidate`     | `causeValidation: false`                     |\n| `dontRunListeners` | none                                         |\n\nTo touch every field before showing errors, call `form.handleSubmit()`, which\nmarks all registered fields as touched. To show errors without touching fields,\nconfigure `errorVisibility` instead.\n\nRead meta from the field API, as `field.meta` in a render prop or with\n`useSelector(field.atom, (state) => state.meta)`. The form API does not look up\nmeta by path.\n\nTo clear meta, `form.resetField(name)` and `field.reset()` reset one field's\nvalue and meta. To clear every field's meta but keep the values the user\nentered, reset the form to its current values without moving the default\nbaseline:\n\n```tsx\nform.reset(form.state.values, { updateDefaultValues: false })\n```\n\nThis also clears form-level errors, submission state, and dirty history.\n\n### On-demand validation\n\nv2 has no public method that validates a single field or every field outside\nsubmission. Express when a field validates through its validators instead:\n\n- Use `triggers` to choose the events that run a validator.\n- Use `watchFields` to rerun a validator when another field changes, which\n  covers most v1 `validateField` calls made from another field's `onChange`.\n- Call `form.handleSubmit()` to validate every field and the form together.\n  Unlike `validateAllFields`, it also calls `onSubmit` when validation passes.\n  It resolves to the error results, so an empty array means everything is\n  valid.\n\n`form.validate('change')` and `form.validate('blur')` still exist, but they run\nform-level validators only. Field validators do not run.\n\n### Errors\n\nv2 does not write error maps directly. Return errors from a validator, or from\n`onSubmit` with `createValidationError(...)` as shown in\n[Errors and submit results](#errors-and-submit-results). For server-rendered\nerrors, pass `serverState` to `useForm`.\n\nTo read errors, `form.state.errors` holds form-level errors only. Errors routed\nto fields stay on the fields, available as `field.errors`. Use\n`form.state.isValid` to check both levels at once.\n\n### Schemas\n\n`parseValuesWithSchema` checked the current values against a schema without\nstoring errors. To keep that behavior, call the schema yourself:\n\n```tsx\nconst result = await schema['~standard'].validate(form.state.values)\n\nif (result.issues) {\n  // handle issues\n}\n```\n\nTo validate with the schema and use its parsed output, add it to `validators`\nand read `schemaOutputs` in `onSubmit`, as described in\n[Standard schemas](#standard-schemas).\n\n## Shared form options\n\nFor extracted components, v1 composition examples often use a custom\n`useAppForm` hook plus `withForm` from `createFormHook`. v2 still supports app\nform hooks, but `withForm` was removed. The smaller building block for shared\ndefaults is `formOptions(...)`:\n\n```tsx\nimport { formOptions } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nexport const sharedFormOptions = formOptions({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    lastName: '',\n    address: {\n      street: '',\n      country: '',\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nconst form = useForm({\n  ...sharedFormOptions,\n  onSubmit: ({ value }) => {\n    console.log(value)\n  },\n})\n```\n\nWhen typing extracted components, prefer the v2 public types covered in\n[Splitting forms](./splitting-forms):\n\n```tsx\nimport type { AnyReactFormApi, FieldWithValue } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nfunction StringField({ field }: { field: FieldWithValue<string> }) {\n  return (\n    <input\n      value={field.value}\n      onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n    />\n  )\n}\n\nfunction SubmitButton({ form }: { form: AnyReactFormApi }) {\n  return (\n    <form.Subscribe selector={(state) => [state.canSubmit, state.isSubmitting]}>\n      {([canSubmit, isSubmitting]) => (\n        <button type=\"submit\" disabled={!canSubmit || isSubmitting}>\n          {isSubmitting ? '...' : 'Submit'}\n        </button>\n      )}\n    </form.Subscribe>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n`AnyReactFormApi` and `FieldWithValue<T>` intentionally erase unrelated type\ndetails for generic UI pieces. Use `ReactFormType<typeof formOpts>` when a\ncomponent needs the option-derived data and field-path surface. Options created\nwith `appFormOptions` also retain their app component map. Submit error types\nmay intentionally widen when the shared options omit `onSubmit` so it can be\nsupplied later. Prefer these aliases over spelling the full `FormApi` or\n`FieldApi` generic lists in application components.\n\nFor components that previously used `withForm`, pass the form API explicitly and\ntype it from the same options object:\n\n```tsx\n// v1\nconst AddressFields = withForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    address: {\n      street: '',\n      country: '',\n    },\n  },\n  render: ({ form }) => (\n    <>\n      <form.Field name=\"address.street\">{/* ... */}</form.Field>\n      <form.Field name=\"address.country\">{/* ... */}</form.Field>\n    </>\n  ),\n})\n```\n\n```tsx\n// v2\nimport { formOptions } from '@tanstack/react-form'\nimport type { ReactFormType } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nexport const profileFormOptions = formOptions({\n  defaultValues: {\n    address: {\n      street: '',\n      country: '',\n    },\n  },\n})\n\ninterface AddressFieldsProps {\n  form: ReactFormType<typeof profileFormOptions>\n}\n\nfunction AddressFields({ form }: AddressFieldsProps) {\n  return (\n    <>\n      <form.Field name=\"address.street\">{/* ... */}</form.Field>\n      <form.Field name=\"address.country\">{/* ... */}</form.Field>\n    </>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Form groups and field groups\n\nReplace v1 form group usage with `form.FormGroup`. It is the v2 tool for\nmulti-step forms and scoped validation when a section is part of one concrete\nform shape:\n\n```tsx\n<form.FormGroup name=\"guestDetails\" onSubmit={() => goToNextStep()}>\n  {(group) => (\n    <>\n      <group.Field name=\"name\">\n        {(field) => (\n          <input\n            value={field.value}\n            onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n          />\n        )}\n      </group.Field>\n      <button type=\"button\" onClick={() => group.handleSubmit()}>\n        Continue\n      </button>\n    </>\n  )}\n</form.FormGroup>\n```\n\nInside the group, field names are scoped. `name=\"name\"` becomes\n`guestDetails.name`, `group.ArrayField name=\"guests\"` becomes\n`guestDetails.guests`, and watched fields are scoped the same way.\n\nGroup submission is its own validation cycle. `group.handleSubmit()` validates\nthe group and its fields and then calls the group's `onSubmit` or\n`onSubmitInvalid`; `form.handleSubmit()` does not also run the group's\nvalidators. Keep any rules required for final whole-form submission in the\nform-level validator pipeline as well. `group.handleSubmit()` resolves to an\nerror array, and `group.state.errors` is an array.\n\nFor a field inside a mounted group, scalar state exposed to `errorVisibility`\n(such as `submissionAttempts` and `isDirty`) is scoped to the nearest group.\nThe callback's `values` and `errors` remain form-wide.\n\nv1's `withFieldGroup` HOC was removed. v2 replaces it with\n`defineFieldGroup(...)` for reusable field bundles. Use it when a component\nshould not care where its fields live in the parent form:\n\n```tsx\nimport { defineFieldGroup } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nconst rangeFieldGroup = defineFieldGroup(({ strict }) => ({\n  lower: strict<string>(),\n  upper: strict<string>(),\n}))\n\nfunction RangeFieldsImpl({\n  fields,\n}: {\n  fields: typeof rangeFieldGroup.fields\n}) {\n  return (\n    <>\n      <fields.Field name=\"lower\">\n        {(field) => (\n          <input\n            value={field.value}\n            onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n          />\n        )}\n      </fields.Field>\n      <fields.Field\n        name=\"upper\"\n        validators={[\n          {\n            triggers: ['change'],\n            watchFields: ['lower'],\n            run: ({ value }) => {\n              const lower = fields.getFieldValue('lower')\n              if (Number(value) < Number(lower)) {\n                return 'Upper bound must be greater than lower bound'\n              }\n            },\n          },\n        ]}\n      >\n        {(field) => (\n          <input\n            value={field.value}\n            onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.target.value)}\n          />\n        )}\n      </fields.Field>\n    </>\n  )\n}\n\nexport const RangeFields = rangeFieldGroup.bindComponent(\n  RangeFieldsImpl,\n  'fields',\n)\n```\n\nThen bind virtual names to concrete paths wherever the group is used:\n\n```tsx\n<RangeFields\n  form={form}\n  fields={{\n    lower: 'minPrice',\n    upper: 'maxPrice',\n  }}\n/>\n```\n\nUse this v2 pattern to migrate v1 `withFieldGroup` components that were reused\nagainst different field paths. If you are using app form components from\n`createFormHook`, wrap components that expect an injected field API with\n`getFormHookHelpers()`, then define field groups with `defineAppFieldGroup`:\n\n```tsx\nimport { createFormHook, getFormHookHelpers } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nconst { fieldComponent } = getFormHookHelpers()\nconst AppTextField = fieldComponent.strict(StringField, 'field')\n\nconst { appFormOptions, useAppForm, defineAppFieldGroup } = createFormHook({\n  fieldComponents: {\n    TextField: AppTextField,\n  },\n  formComponents: {},\n})\n\nconst contactFieldGroup = defineAppFieldGroup(({ strict }) => ({\n  name: strict<string>(),\n}))\n```\n\n## Listeners\n\nv1 listeners were event-keyed objects. v2 listeners use a validator-like array\nshape with `run`, `triggers`, and optional `triggerDebounceMs`. A trigger can be\na string or `{ trigger, when }`, and debounce can be a number or a callback.\nForm listeners support `change`, `blur`, `submit`, `mount`, and `reset`; field\nlisteners additionally support `unmount`.\n\n```tsx\n// v2\n<form.Field\n  name=\"amount\"\n  listeners={[\n    {\n      triggers: ['blur'],\n      run: ({ value, fieldApi }) => {\n        fieldApi.handleChange(Number(value).toFixed(2))\n      },\n    },\n  ]}\n/>\n```\n\nFor cross-field field listeners, put the source fields in `watchFields`. In\n`form.FormGroup` and field-group-bound components, `watchFields` uses the scoped\nor virtual field names and v2 resolves them to the concrete form paths.\nForm-level listeners instead observe propagated events and receive an optional\nsource field as `triggerFieldApi`. It is present for propagated field changes\nand blurs, but absent for form-originated events such as mount, reset, and\nsubmit.\n\n## Server and framework integrations\n\nThe v1 examples include Next server actions, Remix, and TanStack Start examples\nthat use v1's keyed validators and store-level errors. The v2 examples show a\nnew server-validation model in `@tanstack/react-form-start` and a Next.js\nexample with shared isomorphic validation.\n\nKey changes:\n\n- Import `serverValidateHelper` from `@tanstack/react-form`, then import the\n  framework adapter from `@tanstack/react-form-start`,\n  `@tanstack/react-form-nextjs`.\n- Share common form configuration with `formOptions(...)`.\n- Return the `createErrorMap()` map directly from framework/server validators\n  when routing form and field errors.\n- Combine `triggers: ['server']` with `runOnSubmit: false` for a form validator\n  that must run only on the server. Server-triggered validators otherwise still\n  run during client submission because submission is enabled by default.\n- Next.js and Remix adapters, and the Start adapter when no callback override is\n  supplied, resolve to\n  `{ success: true, values, schemaOutputs }` or\n  `{ success: false, serverState }`. Pass the failure's `serverState` back to\n  `useForm({ ...formOpts, serverState })` on the client.\n- `@tanstack/react-form-remix` was removed.\n\nFor example, a Start adapter is configured separately from the shared form\noptions:\n\n```tsx\nimport { serverValidateHelper } from '@tanstack/react-form'\nimport { start } from '@tanstack/react-form-start'\n\nconst { createServerValidate } = serverValidateHelper({\n  framework: start(),\n})\n\nconst serverValidate = createServerValidate(formOpts)\n```\n\nIn `formOpts`, a server-only validator returns its routed error map directly:\n\n```tsx\n{\n  triggers: ['server'],\n  runOnSubmit: false,\n  run: ({ value, createErrorMap }) => {\n    const errors = createErrorMap()\n\n    if (value.age < 13) {\n      errors.fields.age = 'You must be at least 13'\n    }\n\n    return errors\n  },\n}\n```\n\nClient rendering still follows the same v2 field surface:\n\n```tsx\n<form.Field name=\"age\">\n  {(field) => (\n    <>\n      <input\n        name={field.name}\n        value={field.value}\n        onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n        onChange={(event) => field.handleChange(Number(event.target.value))}\n      />\n      {field.errors.map((error) => (\n        <div key={error.message} role=\"alert\">\n          {error.message}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </>\n  )}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\n## Migration order for an app\n\n1. Upgrade imports and keep the smallest possible form compiling with\n   ESM `import` syntax, `useForm`, `defaultValues`, `form.Field`, and\n   `form.handleSubmit()`.\n2. Move every field-level `defaultValue` into form-level `defaultValues` and\n   remove `defaultMeta`.\n3. Update field render props from `field.state.*` to the direct v2 surface.\n4. Replace `useStore(...store...)` with `useSelector(...atom...)`.\n5. Convert validators and listeners to arrays, paying special attention to the\n   default submit behavior.\n6. Convert arrays from `mode=\"array\"` to `form.ArrayField`; keep relative\n   mutators on its render prop or move them to path-based form methods.\n7. Return `createErrorMap(...)` directly from form, group, and server validators,\n   and convert submitted endpoint errors to `createValidationError(...)`.\n8. Revisit composition: use `formOptions(...)` for shared options,\n   `ReactFormType<typeof formOpts>` for extracted form props,\n   `form.FormGroup` for scoped sections, and\n   `defineFieldGroup(...).bindComponent(...)` for reusable field bundles.\n9. Re-run React integration tests around validation timing, field rerenders,\n   groups, server error hydration, and array mutations. These are the areas\n   where v2 intentionally tightened behavior.\n"}
